# btm-x-tok — ALLOWLIST .gitignore
# Published repo = ONLY spec/docs + the two submodules + agent wiring.
# Ignore everything, then re-include exactly the publishable set. Any local
# integration code (monitor/, vendor/, scripts/, Cargo.*, MERGE_PLAN.md, .attic/)
# or future file is ignored by default and cannot be accidentally committed.
#
# Pattern rules: "/*" matches ONLY immediate children of the root ("*" never
# crosses "/"). Git won't descend into an ignored directory, so a directory must
# be re-included ("!/harness/") BEFORE its contents ("!/harness/**").

# 1) default-deny floor (top-level only)
/*

# 2) publishable top-level files
!/.gitignore
!/.gitmodules
!/LICENSE
!/NOTICE
!/README.md
!/AGENTS.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/GEMINI.md

# 3) upstream submodules (gitlinks)
!/bottom
!/tokscale

# 4) the spec directory (dir first so git descends, then all contents)
!/harness/
!/harness/**

# 5) cross-agent wiring pointers (point at AGENTS.md; never duplicate it)
!/.cursor/
!/.cursor/**
!/.github/
!/.github/copilot-instructions.md
